<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish Dec retail sales value falls 0.7 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Irish Dec retail sales value falls 0.7 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The value of Irish retail sales fell a provisional seasonally adjusted 0.7 percent in December, giving a year-on-year increase of 7.9 percent, Central Statistics Office (CSO) data showed on Friday.  </p>
<p>In November retail sales value was up 0.6 percent over the month and rose 8.9 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>			  VALUE OF SALES</p>
<p>	   Index base 1980  Monthly change  Year change</p>
<p>Latest month     136.7	 -0.9	     +7.9</p>
<p>Previous month   138.0	 +0.6	     +8.9</p>
<p>Year ago month   126.7	   -		+5.8</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
